From: Q.W4 Lane F — fleet-wide phantom-class consumer sweep
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cosmetic): retire .glass-{subtle,medium} + .cartoon-card phantom classes

Q.W4 Lane F — fourier-analysis portion. 31 sites across 23 files.
(Corrected at Q.W6: the W6 phantom-class corpus-grep gate caught 2
`.glass-elevated` sites the original 29-site patch missed — see F.1.)

  F.1  11 phantom-glass sites — `.glass-subtle` -> `.glass-wash` (5),
       `.glass-medium` -> `.glass-quiet` (4), `.glass-elevated` ->
       `.glass-floating` (2). Classes retired from glass-ui at the v0.8.0
       ladder rename (`eb9c44c`) / never canonical. Straight template
       class rename. The 2 `.glass-elevated` sites (PaperSearchDropdown
       `.paper-search-results`, EquationView `.coeff-popover`) are both
       floating-overlay surfaces; `floating` is the canonical v0.8.0
       rename target for the `elevated` ladder rung.

  F.2  20 `.cartoon-card` sites across 10 files. The `.cartoon-card`
       *glass-ui* recipe was deleted at C.W5 (`304ac78`); fourier carries a
       LOCAL `.cartoon-card` recipe in `web/src/style.css` (added post-Qψ).
       This patch migrates the 20 call-sites to the idiomatic glass-ui
       component-over-class form:
         - genuine card surfaces  -> `<Card surface="cartoon">`  (18 sites)
         - decoration on a non-card element -> `cartoon-surface` utility
           class (2 sites: MorphShapePreview `<button>`, BasisCanvas
           canvas-host `<div>`).
       After this lands the local `web/src/style.css` `.cartoon-card` block
       (4 rules, ~20 lines) is dead and fourier should delete it — see the
       handoff note in W4-Lane-F-phantom-sweep.md.

APPLY-BASE: this diff is computed against the fourier-analysis WORKING TREE
as of glass-ui Q.W4 (fourier worktree carries ~100 files of in-flight WIP;
the 9 phantom-glass sites exist ONLY in that WIP, not at committed HEAD
926ca6a). The fourier team applies this AFTER committing their WIP:
  git apply --recount --3way docs/.../W4-Lane-F-fourier.patch
(`--recount` tolerates hand-authored hunk line-count drift; verified clean
with `git apply --check --recount` against the fourier worktree at Q.W4.)
A HEAD-targeted patch is infeasible (the phantom-glass corpus is not at HEAD).

